        their logic).
        \n\n
        \"Stable\" releases are published on a monthly schedule. While it is named \"stable\"
        due to being extensively tested, it is often \"stale\" and prone to external breakage.
        \n\n
        \"Nightly\" releases are published before midnight on any day that sees changes to the
        codebase of YtDlp. This is the RECOMMENDED channel.
        \n\n
        \"Master\" provides the latest fixes and features, but may be prone to bugs or regressions.
